🧩 Daily 2-Hour Structure
Use this EVERY day:
45 min → Learn concept
45 min → Code / design
30 min → Explain aloud (VERY IMPORTANT)

What Interviewers Will Look For (Staff Level)
They don’t care if you “know everything”. They care if you can:
1. Go Deep
“How does mutex work internally?”
“What happens in kernel on syscall?”
2. Design Tradeoffs
Why REST vs gRPC?
Why eventual consistency?
3. Ownership Thinking
Scaling
Failure handling
Monitoring
⚠️ Common Mistakes (Avoid These)
❌ Only watching tutorials (no coding)
❌ Ignoring system design depth
❌ Not practicing explanation
❌ Shallow cloud knowledge

